  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Asymptotics of Plancherel measures for symmetric groups — We consider the asymptotics of the Plancherel mea- sures on partitions of n as n goes to inﬁnity.\n\n**Asymptotics of Plancherel measures for symmetric groups**\n\n*SYMMETRIC GROUPS*\n\n43 pp, 23 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We consider the asymptotics of the Plancherel mea- sures on partitions of n as n goes to inﬁnity. We prove that the local structure of a Plancherel typical partition in the middle of the limit shape converges to a determinantal point process with the discrete sine kernel. On the edges of the limit shape, we prove that the joint distri- bution of suitably scaled 1st, 2nd, and so on rows of a Plancherel typical diagram converges to the corresponding distribution for eigenvalues of random Hermitian matrices (given by the Airy ker- nel). This proves a conjecture due to Baik, Deift, and Johansson by methods diﬀerent from the Riemann-Hilbert techniques used in their original papers [2, 3] and from the combinatorial proof given in [23].\n\n**Outline.** 1.1 Plancherel measures; 1 Introduction; 1.2 Poissonization and correlation functions; 1.3 Asymptotics in the bulk of the spectrum; 1.4 Behavior near the edge of the spectrum and; 1.5 Poissonization and depoissonization; 1.6 Organization of the paper; 1.7 Acknowledgements; 2 Correlation functions of the measures $M^\\th; 2.1 Proof of Theorem; 2.2 Proof of Theorem; 2.4 Commuting difference operator; 3 Correlation functions in the bulk of the spe; 3.1 Proof of Theorem; 4 Edge of the spectrum: convergence to the Air; 4.1 Results and strategy of proof; 4.2 Proof of Theorem; 4.3 Depoissonization and proof of Theorem",
      "lang": "en",
